2026-04-06 14:16:39 - Agent_20260406140659 - INFO - [+] Agent signaled completion: Reviewed 3 CodeQL findings related to SQL filter expression compilation from user-controlled subscription data in RocketMQ broker. All three findings involve user-controlled data flowing to FilterFactory.INSTANCE.get(type).compile(expression), which calls SelectorParser.parse() - a JMS SQL92 grammar parser. The parser is constrained (AND/OR/comparisons only, no arbitrary Java method calls), so this is NOT arbitrary code execution. The risks are: DoS via complex expressions, cache pollution (PARSE_CACHE max 100 entries), and potential parser vulnerabilities. Finding 1 (ConsumerFilterManager.build line 94) is via HEART_BEAT network requests; Finding 2 (ConsumerFilterManager.decode line 249) is from persisted config file; Finding 3 (ClientManageProcessor.checkClientConfig line 206) is the most directly network-accessible path, guarded by enablePropertyFilter=false default. All submitted as manual review (mr) with medium severity since they warrant closer inspection for DoS potential and the specific nature of the SQL92 parser's safety guarantees.
